# Working with {{ project_name }}

This is a Django internal management application generated from
`mgaitan/django-unfold-copier-template`.

## Project Shape

- Django settings live in `{{ project_slug }}/config/settings/`.
- The primary CRUD surface is Django admin styled with `django-unfold`.
- `/` redirects to `/admin/`; the admin is the application shell.
- The sample app is `{{ project_slug }}/apps/core/`.
- Tests live in `{{ project_slug }}/tests/`.
- Project-specific skills live in `.agents/skills/`.

## Commands

```bash
make install
make migrate
make seed
make run
make qa
```

## Django Guidelines

- Prefer Django admin + Unfold for model management before building custom CRUD.
- Keep custom views private and integrated into the admin/Unfold experience.
- Only the admin login should be public by default.
- Keep settings environment-specific and avoid production secrets in git.
- Use `select_related`/`prefetch_related` in admin querysets when adding relation-heavy models.
- Add focused pytest coverage for model behavior, permissions, and custom views.

## Unfold Guidelines

- Admin classes should inherit from `unfold.admin.ModelAdmin`.
- Use Unfold filters from `unfold.contrib.filters.admin` for compact changelists.
- Keep the default light theme with brand color `{{ brand_color }}` unless the product identity changes.
- Avoid enabling global overlays or command palettes unless explicitly requested.
- When adding a model, register it in admin with `list_display`, `search_fields`, `list_filter`, and sensible fieldsets.

## QA

Before handing off changes, run:

```bash
make qa
```
